By including these additional properties into the contract testing, you can verify the behavior of your method using both internal and external properties of your data.

You can also add additional properties (like Count, LastIndexOf, Contains) to test the result and verify other behaviors that may not immediately be apparent from the given tests. 

Each line of PexContractAssert.cs file is a separate condition that your method must satisfy. The `PexObserve.ValueForViewing` method is used to log the values of different variables for debugging purposes. The `Assert.IsTrue` method is used to verify that each condition holds true for a given set of inputs.--------------------            
            if (Old_arrListCount > 0 && New_Ret < 0) 
