```
In the test, we are providing `AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true)` in the test as we are not assuming anything for now. 

The test checks the IndexOf method contract. 
We are using `PexObserve.ValueForViewing` and `Assert.AreEqual` to check if the count of `ArrayList` and the output of the IndexOf method after adding an element remains the same. 

We are then breaking the execution for each index of `ArrayList` that gives a value of `0`, as the `IndexOf(int )` method does not work as expected when its ArrayList size is zero.

```
if (Old_arrListCount == 0 && New_Ret == 0) 
{
    Assert.AreEqual(0,0);
}
```
Then, for each index of `ArrayList` that gives a value of `-1`, also, by breaking the execution and using the `Assert.AreEqual`, we verify that the count and the LastIndexOf and Contains methods of the `ArrayList` remain the same, as expected.

```
if (New_Ret == -1) 
{
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount, New_arrListCount);
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListContainsX, New_arrListContainsX);
}
```
If none of the above conditions matches, then the test verifies `New_Ret value`, `Old_arrListLastIndexOfX` and `Old_arrListContainsX` remain the same.
```xml
Assert.AreEqual(New_Ret, Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
Assert.AreEqual(true, Old_arrListContainsX);
```

The contract ensures the behavior of the `IndexOf(int)` method.--------------------